; A rule and a copy of it with its unknowns renamed are one rule: a program is
; a set of rules up to the names of their unknowns.  So every eats the one
; token, as it would with the rule written once, and unique sees one match.
(tok 1)
(rule eat (take (tok $x)) (make (ate $x)))
(rule eat-again (take (tok $y)) (make (ate $y)))
